<Base
	Title="APHRODITE // CCR COMPRESSION ENGINE"
	Description={`Context management for tool-using AI agents. Aphrodite turns verbose tool output - logs, diffs, files, searches, JSON, and browser snapshots - into compact, retrievable previews. Up to ${Benchmark.Ceiling} compression on the standard corpus (${Benchmark.Overall} overall), ${Benchmark.LatencyHeadline} end-to-end.`}
>
	<PageShell Rhythm="hero">
		<!-- HERO SLAB -->
		<!-- SHARED-SLOT NOTE: PageHeader (t_130e5ed4) is deliberately NOT used on
		     this page. PageHeader renders its own <h1>; the landing's <h1> is the
		     stamped wordmark below, which is the page's identity, so a swap would
		     ship two h1s and shrink the wordmark from 144px to 48px. The lead below
		     keeps PageHeader's rhythm - one sentence, one <p>. -->
		<!-- SIX BANDS, ONE RULE. Bands 02-06 are `.band`, whose chapter rule is
		     `--oxblood-dark`; `.blueprint-section`'s default is the grey
		     `--blueprint-rule`. Band 01 therefore states the same crimson through
		     the documented knob, so the six numbered bands open on one rule and a
		     reader can see the chapter grammar before the second band repeats it. -->
		<header
			class="blueprint-section relative flex w-full flex-col items-start justify-start pt-4 text-start"
			style="--blueprint-rule: var(--oxblood-dark)"
			data-enter
		>
			<!-- Beat 01. The folio, in the published blueprint voice: six of these
			     number the six chapters, and each is quiet on purpose - a chapter
			     number is navigation, not decoration. -->
			<p class="section-index !mb-10">01 // POSITIONING</p>
			<!-- Brand card: the red aphrodite.svg mark in the crimson module,
			     oxblood offset underlay (user instruction: the red mark everywhere).
			     The card's 24-unit drop to the wordmark was the ceremonial stack
			     this beat was paying for: the product's own name now follows its
