						</span>
						M+ TOKENS SAVED
					</span>
					<span class="max-w-[15rem] text-pretty text-base leading-relaxed text-oxblood-dark">
						{Study.Sessions} real sessions, {Study.ApiCalls} API calls, {Study.Measured}
						.
					</span>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- BEAT 05 // INTEGRATION - two paths, and the difference between them is
		     stated rather than implied: one lives inside the turn, the other speaks
		     HTTP. The wording is /hermes/'s and /plugin/'s own, not a second
		     description of the same thing.

		     THE PAGE'S QUIET BAND. 02 and 03 are the two dense bands (a plate
		     plus prose plus a fold; five paragraphs plus a card cluster) and 06
		     is the panel the reader acts on. Drawn as two filled plates, this
		     band was a third and fourth heavy box in a row, so the page had no
		     valley between the evidence spread and the install panel. The lanes
		     are the same two lanes with the same words and the same links -
		     drawn as ruled columns instead of plates, with the chapter distance
		     above them. Nothing was cut to buy the air; the band simply stops
		     filling its own background. -->
		<section class="band relative w-full" data-reveal>
			<p class="section-index">05 // CONNECT</p>
			<h2 class="type-section mb-6 text-bone-white">Two ways to run it</h2>
			<div class="prose-flow max-w-[62ch]">
				<p class="type-body text-bone-newsprint">
					Both lanes run the same engine over the same CCR store. One is a native plugin
					inside Hermes, where the interception lives inside the turn; the other is a
					listener on a port, where it can only see traffic that arrives over HTTP.
				</p>
			</div>
			<!-- THE DECISION MATRIX - the band's composition, and the reason this
			     chapter is CONNECT rather than a second pair of plates. Four axes
			     down the side, the two lanes across, one row per axis. Ruled rows
			     rather than a <table>: every cell holds a sentence, and a sentence
			     in a table cell wraps against a fixed track.
			     The two lane columns below are the SOURCE these cells compress -
			     every cell is a fact its own lane's prose already states, so the
			     matrix may summarise a sentence and may never carry a claim the
			     prose does not make. The stack repeats the lane name above each
			     cell on small screens, because a stack loses the column header
			     that named it. -->
			<div class="grunge shell-card mt-10" data-grunge data-grunge-mode="edge">
				<div
					class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 border-b border-[color:var(--tier-shell-edge)] bg-soot-black px-4 py-3 sm:px-5"
				>
					<span class="telemetry-tag telemetry-tag--crimson shadow-[2px_2px_0px_#000]">
						THE DECISION MATRIX
					</span>
					<span class="grow font-mono text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-dust">
						one engine, two lanes - what each one sees, shares, and cannot do
					</span>
				</div>
				<div class="px-4 sm:px-5">
					<div
						class="hidden border-b border-[color:var(--tier-shell-edge)] py-3 lg:grid lg:grid-cols-[13rem_1fr_1fr] lg:gap-10"
					>
						<span class="type-meta font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-zinc-dust">AXIS</span>
						<span class="type-meta font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-bone-white">
							PATH 01 // NATIVE PLUGIN
						</span>
						<span class="type-meta font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-bone-white">
							PATH 02 // OPENAI-COMPATIBLE PROXY
						</span>
					</div>
					{Decision.map((Row) => (
						<div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 border-b border-[color:var(--tier-shell-edge)] py-5 last:border-b-0 lg:grid-cols-[13rem_1fr_1fr] lg:gap-10">
							<p class="type-meta font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-zinc-dust">
								{Row.Axis}
							</p>
							<div>
								<p class="type-meta mb-2 font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-zinc-dust lg:hidden">
									PATH 01 // NATIVE PLUGIN
								</p>
								<p class="type-body text-bone-newsprint">{Row.One}</p>
							</div>
							<div>
								<p class="type-meta mb-2 font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-zinc-dust lg:hidden">
									PATH 02 // OPENAI-COMPATIBLE PROXY
								</p>
								<p class="type-body text-bone-newsprint">{Row.Two}</p>
