<style>
	/* ONE GUTTER FOR EVERY BAND - AND IT IS THE SHELL'S OWN.
	   `PageShell` insets `<main>` by `px-5 sm:px-8 lg:px-14` (20 / 32 / 56px),
	   and every band on the page is a `w-full` child of that `<main>`, so the
	   bands already share one left edge with no padding of their own. The
	   defect the phase-2 review measured (sections 02/03/05/06 flush at the
	   band edge while the evidence spread was inset) came from the one band
	   that ADDED padding, not from the five that had none.

	   The first fix applied that extra padding to every band instead, which
	   aligned the six bands with each other and moved the whole page 56px
	   right of every other route: measured at 1440, `/setup/`, `/showcase/`
	   and `/docs/` put their first glyph at x=56 while `/` put it at x=112,
	   so navigating between routes shifted the page sideways. Two nested
	   paddings that happen to sum to a constant is not one gutter; the shared
	   edge is the shell's, applied once. Verified at 1440: all six bands plus
	   the related nav and the colophon report textX=56, inset=0.

	   Nothing is page-scoped any more, so nothing can drift: a band that
	   wants air uses margin on its own plate (`mx-3` on the stage plate
	   exists for the tilt's bounding box, not for a gutter). */

	/* THE BONE SPREAD IS A SPREAD, NOT A BOX. The evidence band is the page's
	   only surface change, and its light ground used to be exactly the text
	   column (x 56 to 1383 at 1440), so the kicker's glyph sat 0px from the
	   paper's edge and the 26.9% numeral 5px from it - while every other
	   surface on the page insets its text (the demo plate 55px, the install
	   panel 44px). A light rectangle that ends where the text ends reads as a
	   text box, not as paper.

	   The ground therefore bleeds to the shell's box edges while the TEXT
	   stays on the page's one gutter: the margin is negative by exactly the
	   padding it adds back, so the net text position is unchanged (verified:
	   textX 56 at 1440, 32 at 768, 20 at 390 - identical to the five dark
	   bands) and only the surface grows. The values are PageShell's own scale
	   (`px-5 sm:px-8 lg:px-14`), restated because a child cannot read its
	   parent's utility. */
	.paper-band {
		margin-inline: -1.25rem;
		padding-inline: 1.25rem;
	}

	@media (min-width: 40rem) {
		.paper-band {
			margin-inline: -2rem;
			padding-inline: 2rem;
		}
	}

	@media (min-width: 64rem) {
		.paper-band {
			margin-inline: -3.5rem;
			padding-inline: 3.5rem;
		}
	}

	/* One measure for every prose line on the page. Per-container classes were
	   not enough: the install panel is 896px wide, so its paragraphs measured
	   808px (~90 characters) even after the outer blocks were capped. 40rem is
	   ~71 characters at this body size - `ch` is useless here because it
	   measures the "0" glyph, which in DM Sans is far wider than average
	   lowercase (62ch computed to 763px). */
	:global(main p.type-body),
	:global(main li.type-body) {
		max-width: 40rem;
	}
	/* An inline identifier inside a sentence must not break mid-token:
	   `hermes --version` split across two lines reads as `hermes -` / `-version`.
	   A code span is one word, so it wraps as one word or not at all. */
	:global(main code.type-code) {
		white-space: nowrap;
	}
	/* STAGE IDENTITY // the four stages are four different operations, and a
	   reader has to be able to tell stage 03 from stage 01 at a glance and to
	   match it to the same stage on the case study. The accent is therefore one
	   custom property per card: the left edge, the rule, the corner stamp, the
	   heading and the chip all read it, so the five cannot drift apart.

	   01 CLASSIFY           teal     the technical voice: naming the content
	   02 ENRICH & PREVIEW   canary   the result the reader acts on
	   03 BLAKE3 STORE       blood    storage, and the marker it hands back
	   04 AGENT DECIDES      bone     the one step that is the agent's own choice

	   Emphasis is untouched: no shadow, no tilt, no tape, straight edges. The
	   identity is colour + stage letter + figure; the volume stays low.

	   The ink is the accent everywhere except stage 03, where the accent cannot
	   be read as text: --raw-blood measures 2.12:1 on --carbon-void, so its
	   labels are the same hue lifted toward --bone-newsprint (55/45 = 4.85:1).
	   The edge and the rule keep the full raw blood - only the words are
	   lifted. */
	/* The selectors name the tier they override (`.emphasis-quiet`) because
	   Astro scopes page styles with `:where(.astro-...)`, which contributes NO
	   specificity - a bare `.stage-card` would tie with `.emphasis-quiet` and
	   the winner would depend on stylesheet order. `.emphasis-quiet.stage-card`
	   is one class heavier, so the accent wins wherever the sheets land. */
	/* The plate is a TINTED surface, not a transparent one and not a flat dark
	   one. Two failures taught this: transparent made the cards inherit the
	   page (#09090b) so they read as borders on nothing, and a #050506 fill was
	   a 4-level step nobody can see. The fill is the stage accent at 7% over
	   --carbon-void: every card separates from the page AND from its siblings,
	   so the row reads as four plates with four identities before any border
	   is noticed. */
	.emphasis-quiet.stage-card {
		--stage-accent: var(--blood-crimson);
		--stage-ink: var(--stage-accent);
		--stage-tint: 7%;
		background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--stage-accent) var(--stage-tint), var(--carbon-void));
		border-width: 1px;
		border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--stage-accent) 30%, var(--oxblood-dark));
		border-left-width: 2px;
		border-left-color: var(--stage-accent);
	}

	/* FOUR METRICS IN ONE ROW. The published `.metric` is one figure per section;
	   the stage row deliberately spends four, because these four figures are one
	   comparison and not four monuments. So the cap lives on the CARD, not on the
	   class: at the published clamp a card of ~212px would print
	   `aphrodite_retrieve` wider than its own plate, and the figure the reader is
	   meant to compare would be the one that broke the row. The `<wbr>` in stage
	   04 keeps the identifier breakable at its own seam. */
	.stage-card .metric {
		font-size: clamp(1.375rem, 2.2vw, 2rem);
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
	}

	.emphasis-quiet.stage-card--a {
		--stage-accent: var(--weathered-teal);
	}

	.emphasis-quiet.stage-card--b {
		--stage-accent: var(--stamped-canary);
	}

	.emphasis-quiet.stage-card--c {
		--stage-accent: var(--raw-blood);
		--stage-ink: color-mix(in srgb, var(--raw-blood) 55%, var(--bone-newsprint));
	}

	/* Stage 04 is the agent's own decision, which sits outside the engine's
	   three-hue language - so it takes the lightest neutral the palette owns and
	   carries it at a stronger tint (16% vs 7%). At 7% the bone accent was
	   achromatic AND low-contrast: the plate needed a second look to separate.
	   Raised, it reads as the fourth plate of the set rather than as default
	   foreground. */
	.emphasis-quiet.stage-card--d {
		--stage-accent: var(--bone-white);
		--stage-tint: 16%;
	}

	.stage-ink {
		color: var(--stage-ink);
	}

	.stage-rule {
		border-top-color: var(--stage-accent);
	}
</style>
